.max-w-prose
  = doc_info(url: "https://guides.rubyonrails.org/caching_with_rails.html", icon: "archive-box", icon_css: "text-accent") do
    :markdown
      _Loco_**Motion** apps render HTML on the server, and in the Rails 8 /
      Hotwire era that makes **view caching** matter again — with Solid Cache
      in the box, there is nothing extra to run.

.prose
  :markdown
    # View Caching

    A decade of "put Redis in front of everything" advice has left view
    caching with a reputation for complexity it no longer deserves. Rails 8
    ships a database-backed cache store by default, Hotwire has moved
    rendering back to the server where fragments can be reused, and
    ViewComponent has finally learned how to participate. This guide covers
    the modern toolkit — fragment, collection, and HTTP caching, component
    caching, the Turbo interplay, and the stores — and, just as importantly,
    when to leave a view uncached.

- # The roadmap: nine sections plus the victory lap. The links opt out of
- # Turbo because the layout wraps pages in a turbo-frame, which would
- # otherwise swallow same-page anchor jumps.
